From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:54:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] claude bridge: a saved session cut short of its last line is
 not resumed (#4407)

Claude Code writes its session file as it goes. A run shelved for its
conversation's next turn is stopped the moment it is shelved (keepIdle
shelves and SIGTERMs in one pass), so its file can be left without the
last lines its agent held and its process never got to write. unshelve
only checked the file was there (saved), so the conversation's next
turn went on from the file as it stood, told only the messages since:
the run's Claude Code asked Anthropic from a history that was no longer
in the session, and answered with a context a fraction of the client's
(#4407: a 467,984-token turn answered from a 2,171-token one, no
compaction boundary in between).

shelve now records the uuid of the last line of the session the run's
Claude Code said it wrote (noteLines has it), and unshelve refuses a
session whose file does not have that line, its file removed: the turn
is told the whole conversation, as a first one would be. Sessions whose
run named no line (a reply with no tool calls) are not checked, and a
session the check cannot read goes on as before -- a --resume Claude
Code refuses is answered the way start already answers it.

